# Keycloak SPI

- Compile against Keycloak SPI artifacts with Maven `provided` scope. Do not bundle Keycloak into provider JARs.
- Prefer public Keycloak session/event APIs. Authenticator modules may use `keycloak-services` as `provided` for supported base classes (`UsernamePasswordForm`, `AbstractActionTokenHandler`, `EmailTemplateProvider`). Do not shade those APIs into the JAR.
- Keep `${keycloak.version}` in the root POM as the single version override point. Do not invent Maven profiles per Keycloak version; use `-Dkeycloak.version=<version>`.
- For `last-login-timestamp`: listen to `EventType.LOGIN` only unless docs and tests are updated intentionally for a broader contract.
- Treat last-login attribute writes as advisory, best-effort, and non-blocking for authentication. Preserve WARN-only failure logging on the update path.
- For `magic-link`: keep browser-flow scope (no REST mint API unless explicitly requested); preserve LOGIN-capable action-token handlers, theme-resources templates, and the factory-injected customization extension points (`AbstractMagicLinkAuthenticatorFactory` + `MagicLinkCustomizationProvider`).
- When changing supported Keycloak versions, keep root POM default, CI matrix, and provider READMEs aligned.
